35,2,1,talk,Midori,,It seems we have a habit of letting support fall through the cracks and letting our project scopes expire almost immediately.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The physical reality is grim. Our hardware is a mess, and trying to cut over during peak season is a disaster.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"As I feared, we have systems that are essentially frozen in time because we can't test upgrades, and external data moves leave lasting scars.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing the people who actually understand our systems, and the field staff simply ignore training that doesn't fit their routine.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The board loves capital spend but ignores the creeping cost of separate licenses. Bundled pricing is the only thing that stayed stable.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, if bundled pricing is safer, we should avoid modular systems that allow vendors to hike individual component costs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Misaki, if the staff ignores trainers, we need a vendor who stays on-site rather than just sending a manual.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, a fixed configuration might stop the scope from drifting, but it could also lead to the ""aging in place"" I'm worried about.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, I agree. We need someone who sees the depot floor, not just a remote consultant.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, I'd rather have a system that is slightly rigid but financially predictable than a ""flexible"" one that bills us forever.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,We need a single point of accountability. A fragmented support model is a non-starter for me.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,And it must be deployable without killing our November-January window.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,I'm wary of any partner-led migration. The 2018 move proves that external teams often miss the nuances.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,We need a solution that doesn't require a massive hiring surge for administrators we can't find.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Let's prioritize a vendor with a clear, all-in cost structure and a unified support team.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
