60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Meridian's fixed configuration and regional team sound stable, but Corvus's modularity is exactly the billing nightmare Benjamin warned about.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Anchor is the only one with an engineering team present through rollout. That's the only way to survive our yards.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Tessera relies on a partner firm for migration. Given the 2018 disaster, that's a huge risk. Anchor's on-premise approach is safer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Anchor's on-site presence helps the supervisors, but Meridian's hosted suite might be easier on our dwindling admin staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Meridian's fixed configuration and hosted suite suggest the price stability I'm looking for. Corvus is a financial minefield.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, would Anchor's on-site team be able to handle the peak-season freeze?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Likely, because they'd be there to see the chaos in real-time. Meridian's regional team is too distant.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, Anchor is on our own servers. Doesn't that mean we're back to the upgrade problems I found?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"It does. If we can't hire admins, we can't maintain Anchor's servers. Meridian or Tessera are better for staffing.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, maintenance is a known cost. The unknown is the ""application marketplace"" of Tessera. That sounds like a hidden fee trap.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm leaning toward Meridian. A regional service team is better than a partner firm or a fragmented modular mess.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I can't trust a hosted system to work with our yard devices. Anchor is the only practical choice for the floor.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,I'll go with Anchor. I'd rather have engineers on-site than a partner firm that leaves us with mismatched codes.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I'm torn, but the admin shortage is critical. I'll vote Meridian to get the hosting burden off our plates.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Meridian offers the most financial predictability. I'm voting for them.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Stability and accountability over everything.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I still think we're ignoring the yard, but I'll stick to my guns.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'll stick with Anchor.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Meridian it is.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Let's vote.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
